# RAW TRACES ARE NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# A raw strace of a real agent is a capture of an AUTHENTICATED session. Ours
# contained an OAuth token fragment in a captured buffer:
# strace -s 64 truncates each buffer at 64 bytes, but 64 bytes of an
# Authorization header is still 64 bytes of a credential.
#
# docs/trace-format.md already states the rule -- "real captures never carry
# payload bytes out of the machine that made them" -- and the .jsonl records
# honour it (payload_prefix is null in all 46). The raw strace does not, and
# it is the file that would have leaked.
#
# Keep raw traces local. Commit the derived .jsonl and .summary.json, which
# are the evidence anyone else actually needs.
*.strace
*.strace.gz
*.strace.xz
data/gate/*.raw

# benchmark output
results/

